**Good to know:**

-   It runs on Windows, macOS and Linux, and works offline.
-   It is designed for **one person at a time**. Teams take turns on a project or merge copies later (see [Working in a team](ref-teamwork.qmd)).
-   It aims to follow the **REFI-QDA** exchange standard, so projects can move to and from tools such as NVivo, ATLAS.ti and MAXQDA, with some limits.
-   It is licensed under the LGPL v3. If you use it in coursework or research, cite it (the citation is on the QualCoder website).

The simplest route is a ready-made installer from the [releases page](https://github.com/ccbogel/QualCoder/releases). Choose the one appropriate for your laptop.

| System | What to download | What to expect on first launch |
|----|----|----|
| Windows | The Windows installer (.exe) | A SmartScreen warning, because the app is not signed. Click **More info**, then **Run anyway**. |
| macOS | The .dmg file | A Gatekeeper warning. Allow the app under **System Settings \> Privacy & Security**. |
| Linux (Debian/Ubuntu) | The Linux executable, or run from source | Usually no warning. |

**Optional extras (which won't be covered during this workshop)**

-   **VLC** media player is needed to code audio and video
-   **ffmpeg** lets QualCoder draw audio waveforms.

Please note that Audio and video do not work on Fedora Linux.

## Basic Settings

Open **Project \> Settings** (or the settings icon). Only four settings matter for a first session.

\<FIXME - ADD SCREENSHOT\>

1.  **Coder name:** Every code you apply is stamped with your coder name. Set your own name (or initials) before you start, using the **Change** button. This matters later if you compare coding with a collaborator.
2.  **Language:** English is the default. French, German and Spanish are kept up to date; other languages are contributed by volunteers.
3.  **Font and display:** Increase the font size if text is hard to read on a projector or small screen.
4.  **Backups"** QualCoder can back up your project every hour and keep the most recent copies, named like *projectname_BKP_yyyymmdd_hh.qda*. Let's leave this on!

**Behind the scenes:** QualCoder keeps its settings file (`config.ini`) and a log file in a hidden `.qualcoder` folder in your home directory. Remember: do not store project data there!

